{"the_interpretability_of_predictions": "The interpretability of predictions refers to the ability to understand and explain the reasoning behind the outcomes or results generated by a predictive model. In the context of financial statement fraud detection, it is crucial for auditors and other stakeholders to comprehend the factors and indicators that contribute to the model's predictions in order to make informed decisions and take appropriate actions."},
