{"a_combination_of_measures_such_as_accuracy_sensitivity_specificity_precision_and_f1_score": "A combination of measures such as accuracy, sensitivity, specificity, precision, and F1-score refers to a set of performance metrics used to evaluate the effectiveness of fraud detection models. Accuracy measures the overall correctness of the model, sensitivity (or recall) indicates the proportion of actual fraud cases correctly identified, specificity shows the proportion of actual non-fraud cases correctly identified, precision reflects the proportion of predicted fraud cases that are actually fraudulent, and F1-score is a harmonic mean of precision and sensitivity, providing a balance between the two."},
