{"svm_lr_and_ann": "SVM (Support Vector Machine), LR (Logistic Regression), and ANN (Artificial Neural Network) are machine learning models commonly used for classification tasks. SVM is known for its effectiveness in high-dimensional spaces, LR is a statistical method for binary classification, and ANN is a computational model inspired by the human brain, capable of learning complex patterns."},
