{"svm_a_secondary_choice_for_practitioners": "SVM, or Support Vector Machine, is a popular machine learning model known for its effectiveness in classification tasks. However, due to its complexities in configuration, it is often considered a secondary choice for practitioners when compared to other models like tree-based algorithms or deep neural networks."},
{"ann__show__less_impressive_predictive_performance": "The predicate \"show\" in this context indicates the demonstration or revelation of a particular characteristic or performance metric of the ANN model when applied to fraud detection using financial data."},
{"less_impressive_predictive_performance": "\"Less impressive predictive performance\" describes the outcome where the ANN model, when compared to other models like RF, XGB, LR, and SVM, does not achieve the highest accuracy or AUC scores in predicting fraud. Despite this, ANNs are noted for their efficiency in terms of sensitivity."},
