{"modeling_results__start_with__purely_textual_input_txt": "The phrase \"start with\" indicates the initial point or the first condition under which the modeling results are evaluated. It suggests a sequential approach where the evaluation begins with one type of input and then progresses to more complex inputs."},
{"purely_textual_input_txt": "Purely textual input (TXT) represents the simplest form of input data used in the modeling process. It consists solely of text without any additional enhancements or supplementary data, such as financial information. This type of input is used as the baseline for comparing the performance of different models."},
{"modeling_results__continue_with__text_enhanced_by_financial_data_fin_txt": "The phrase \"continue with\" indicates a sequential progression in the modeling process, where the analysis moves from one type of input data to another, specifically from purely textual input to text enhanced with financial data."},
{"text_enhanced_by_financial_data_fin_txt": "Text enhanced by financial data (FIN+TXT) represents a type of input data used in the modeling process that combines textual information with financial data. This enriched input is intended to provide a more comprehensive dataset for the machine learning models, potentially leading to improved performance metrics."},
{"txt_modeling": "TXT modeling refers to the process of using purely textual input for creating models, as opposed to text enhanced by additional data like financial information. It focuses on the analysis and utilization of textual content for predictive or analytical purposes."},
{"txt_modeling__includes__two_new_dl_methods_han_and_gpt_2": "The term 'includes' in this context signifies the incorporation or addition of specific elements into the TXT modeling process. It indicates that certain components or methods are part of the modeling approach."},
{"two_new_dl_methods_han_and_gpt_2": "The two new DL methods, HAN (Hierarchical Attention Networks) and GPT-2 (Generative Pre-trained Transformer 2), are advanced machine learning techniques included in the TXT modeling. These methods utilize pre-trained embeddings and are designed to enhance the modeling process by leveraging complex patterns and structures within the textual data."},
{"traditional_benchmarks": "Traditional benchmarks refer to established evaluation metrics or standard tests used in a particular field to measure performance or effectiveness. In the context of modeling results, these benchmarks serve as a baseline for comparing new methods or models against existing ones."},
{"traditional_benchmarks__take__tf_idf_transformations_of_word_input": "The verb \"take\" in this context signifies the utilization or adoption of a specific method or input by traditional benchmarks. It indicates that these benchmarks incorporate or rely on a certain type of data transformation or feature extraction technique as part of their evaluation process."},
{"tf_idf_transformations_of_word_input": "TF-IDF (Term Frequency-Inverse Document Frequency) transformations of word input represent a common technique used in text analysis to assess the importance of words within a document relative to a collection of documents. By applying TF-IDF transformations, traditional benchmarks can evaluate the relevance and significance of words in textual data, aiding in the assessment of modeling performance."},
{"dl_models": "DL models refer to deep learning models that are used in the context of processing textual input, such as HAN and GPT-2, which are part of the TXT modeling approach.|Here is another description: DL models refer to deep learning models, which are advanced computational algorithms designed to learn and make decisions based on large datasets. These models are particularly effective in tasks requiring pattern recognition and complex decision-making processes.|Here is another description: DL models refer to deep learning models, which are a subset of machine learning algorithms designed to learn and make decisions based on data. In the context of fraud detection, these models are employed to analyze complex patterns and relationships within data to identify potential fraudulent activities."},
