{"solely_linguistic_information": "'Solely linguistic information' refers to the exclusive use of data related to language, such as word frequency counts and readability metrics, in the LING models. This type of information is distinct from other data types, like financial data, that are used in more complex models."},
{"linguistic_information": "Linguistic information refers to data and metrics derived from the analysis of language, including various aspects such as word usage, syntax, and semantic relationships. In the context of modeling, it serves as a foundational input that can enhance the understanding and processing of textual content."},
{"linguistic_information__includes__frequency_counts_of_word_categories_based_on_lm_word_lists_readability": "The term \"includes\" signifies that the subject encompasses or contains the specified elements. In this context, it indicates that linguistic information is composed of various components, such as frequency counts and readability metrics, which are integral to its definition and application."},
{"frequency_counts_of_word_categories_based_on_lm_word_lists_readability": "Frequency counts of word categories based on LM word lists and readability are specific metrics within linguistic information. Frequency counts measure how often words from certain categories appear in a text, while readability assesses the ease with which a text can be read and understood. These metrics are crucial for analyzing and modeling textual data effectively."},
