{"highest_accuracy_89": "\"Highest accuracy, 89%\" refers to the performance metric of ANN in a particular task or application. It indicates that ANN has achieved an accuracy rate of 89%, which is the highest among the models or methods being compared in the given context."},
{"ann__has__best_f1_and_f2_scores": "The predicate \"has\" in this context signifies that the subject, ANN, possesses or achieves certain qualities or metrics. Specifically, it indicates that ANN attains particular performance scores in the task of fraud detection."},
{"best_f1_and_f2_scores": "The best F1- and F2-scores refer to the performance metrics achieved by the ANN model in the context of fraud detection. F1-score is a measure of a model's accuracy on a dataset, calculated as the harmonic mean of precision and recall. F2-score, on the other hand, places more emphasis on recall than precision, making it suitable for imbalanced datasets where false negatives are more critical. In this context, ANN's achievement of the best F1- and F2-scores underscores its effectiveness and superiority over other models in detecting fraud, especially when considering the practical implications of minimizing false negatives."},
