{"sox": "SOX, or the Sarbanes-Oxley Act, is a United States federal law that set new or enhanced standards for all U.S. public company boards, management, and public accounting firms. It was enacted as a response to a number of major corporate and accounting scandals, and it aims to protect investors by improving the accuracy and reliability of corporate disclosures."},
