{"sox_became_effective": "SOX, or the Sarbanes-Oxley Act, is a United States federal law that set new or enhanced standards for all U.S. public company boards, management, and public accounting firms. Its goal was to protect investors from the possibility of fraudulent accounting activities by corporations."},
