{"the_identification_of_fraudulent_behaviour": "The identification of fraudulent behavior refers to the process of detecting deceitful actions or statements, particularly in textual data. This is crucial in fields like financial auditing where distinguishing between truthful and misleading statements can be complex and requires advanced analytical models."},
{"the_attention_mechanisms_of_the_han": "The attention mechanisms of the HAN refer to the specific components within the Hierarchical Attention Network (HAN) model that focus on understanding and processing text by considering the context and structure of words and sentences.|Here is another description: The attention mechanisms of the Hierarchical Attention Network (HAN) are designed to focus on specific parts of the text that are most relevant to the task at hand, in this case, detecting fraudulent behavior."},
