{"the_attention_mechanisms_of_the_han__enable__the_identification_of_the_words_and_sentences_that_contribute_the_most_in_attributing_the_fraudulent_behaviour": "The predicate 'enable' signifies that the attention mechanisms of the HAN model facilitate or make possible a certain action or outcome, which in this context is the identification of key textual elements indicative of fraud."},
{"the_identification_of_the_words_and_sentences_that_contribute_the_most_in_attributing_the_fraudulent_behaviour": "The identification of the words and sentences that contribute the most in attributing the fraudulent behaviour refers to the process of pinpointing specific textual elements within a document that are most likely to indicate fraudulent activity, based on the attention weights assigned by the HAN model."},
{"han__is_notably_advantageous_in_comparison_to__bow_based_traditional_benchmarks": "The phrase \"is notably advantageous in comparison to\" indicates that HAN offers significant benefits or superior performance when compared to another method, in this case, BOW-based traditional benchmarks."},
{"bow_based_traditional_benchmarks": "BOW-based traditional benchmarks refer to methods that rely on Bag-of-Words approaches, which ignore the specific contextual meanings of words and focus solely on the frequency of words in a text, making them less effective for complex text analysis tasks like fraud detection."},
