{"dl_model": "The DL model refers to a deep learning model, which is a type of machine learning model that uses neural networks with multiple layers to analyze and learn from data. In this context, the DL model is being evaluated for its capability in handling textual data alongside quantitative financial features.|Here is another description: The DL model is a state-of-the-art deep learning model designed to enhance the detection of financial fraud. It is capable of capturing semantic associations and discerning the meanings of different word and phrase combinations, which is a significant improvement over traditional methods like the BOW method.|Here is another description: The DL model is a state-of-the-art deep learning model designed to enhance the detection of financial fraud by analyzing both quantitative and textual data in financial reports. It is capable of capturing semantic associations and understanding the meanings of different word and phrase combinations, unlike traditional methods like BOW.|Here is another description: The DL model refers to a state-of-the-art deep learning model proposed in the paper for advanced financial fraud detection. It is designed to analyze both financial and linguistic information, focusing on the content and context of textual data in annual reports."},
