{"interpreting_textual": "\"Interpreting textual\" refers to the process of analyzing and understanding the meaning or content of text. In the context provided, it involves using the DL model to make sense of textual data, likely to extract meaningful insights or features that can be combined with quantitative financial data for further analysis."},
{"features": "Features in this context refer to specific characteristics or indicators that are observed or analyzed. These features are crucial as they help in identifying potential issues or anomalies.|Here is another description: Features in this context refer to specific characteristics or attributes that are indicative of potential fraud. These features are crucial for identifying irregularities that may suggest fraudulent activity."},
