{"a_comprehensive_evaluation_of_different_modeling_techniques": "The object \"a comprehensive evaluation of different modeling techniques\" refers to the detailed assessment and comparison of various methods used for modeling, specifically within the context of detecting fraud using deep learning techniques. This evaluation is conducted using cost-sensitive metrics to differentiate between the impacts of false alarms and missed fraud cases."},
{"the_evaluation": "The evaluation refers to a comprehensive assessment conducted in the paper to compare different modeling techniques used for processing textual and financial data in the context of fraud detection."},
{"the_evaluation__uses__cost_sensitive_metrics": "The predicate \"uses\" indicates the application or employment of a specific method or metric within the evaluation process to gauge the performance and effectiveness of the modeling techniques."},
{"cost_sensitive_metrics": "Cost-sensitive metrics are evaluation criteria that take into account the varying costs or severities associated with different types of errors, such as false alarms versus missed fraud cases, in the context of fraud detection.|Here is another description: Cost-sensitive metrics are evaluation methods that take into account the varying costs associated with different types of errors in a model. In the context of fraud detection, these metrics are crucial for assessing the performance of models that need to balance between identifying fraudulent activities and minimizing false positives."},
{"cost_sensitive_metrics__account_for__the_different_severities_of_false_alarms_versus_missed_fraud_cases": "The predicate \"account for\" in this context means to consider or take into account the varying levels of impact or cost associated with different types of errors. Specifically, it refers to the need to differentiate between the consequences of false alarms (incorrectly flagging legitimate transactions as fraudulent) and missed fraud cases (failing to detect actual fraudulent transactions)."},
{"the_different_severities_of_false_alarms_versus_missed_fraud_cases": "The different severities of false alarms versus missed fraud cases refer to the varying levels of impact or cost associated with these two types of errors in fraud detection. False alarms can lead to unnecessary investigations and customer dissatisfaction, while missed fraud cases can result in significant financial losses and damage to a company's reputation."},
{"textual_analysis": "Textual analysis is a method used to systematically evaluate and interpret text data. It involves the use of various techniques to extract meaningful insights and patterns from written or spoken language.|Here is another description: Textual analysis refers to the process of examining and interpreting text data to extract meaningful insights. In the context of financial documentation, it involves analyzing the content and context of textual information to uncover potential signals of fraud."},
