{"fraudulent_activities_in_most_cases": "Fraudulent activities in this context refer to deliberate deceptions or misrepresentations carried out by individuals within an organization to gain an unfair or illegal advantage. These activities can include falsifying financial records, misrepresenting company performance, or engaging in other forms of financial misconduct."},
{"social_psychology_research": "Social psychology research is a field of study that examines how individuals' thoughts, feelings, and behaviors are influenced by the actual, imagined, or implied presence of others. In the context of financial documentation, this research can provide insights into the psychological factors that may lead to fraudulent activities."},
