{"importance_weight_per_word_\u03b1it_via_a_softmax_function": "The object is the importance weight per word \u03b1it, which is derived by applying a softmax function to the normalized annotations. This weight signifies the relative importance of each word in the context of the sentence."},
{"word_context_vector_uw": "The word context vector uw is a trainable vector used in the attention mechanism to generate enhanced annotations for words in a sentence. It plays a crucial role in determining the importance weight of each word.|Here is another description: The word context vector uw is a trainable vector used in an attention mechanism to generate enhanced annotations. It is multiplied with newly generated annotations and normalized to produce importance weights for each word."},
{"word_context_vector_uw__initialized__randomly": "The predicate \"initialized\" describes the process by which the word context vector uw is set up at the beginning of the training procedure. This initialization is a necessary step before the vector can be fine-tuned during training."},
{"randomly": "\"Randomly\" describes the manner in which the word context vector uw is initialized. This random initialization ensures that the vector starts with a diverse set of values, allowing for a more effective learning process during training."},
{"word_context_vector_uw__learned__concurrently": "The predicate \"learned\" indicates that the word context vector uw is trained or adjusted during the training procedure of the attention mechanism. This process involves updating the vector to optimize its performance in generating accurate importance weights."},
{"concurrently": "\"Concurrently\" describes the manner in which the word context vector uw is learned. It signifies that the vector is updated and trained simultaneously with other components of the model, ensuring that all parts of the system are optimized together."},
{"importance_weights": "Importance weights are values assigned to each word in a sentence, indicating their relative significance within the context of the sentence. These weights are derived through a softmax function applied to the product of newly generated annotations and a trainable context vector.|Here is another description: Importance weights are values assigned by the attention mechanism to words and sentences, indicating their relative importance in the context of a document. These weights help the HAN model to build a more accurate and context-aware document representation."},
{"importance_weights__concatenated_with__already_computed_context_annotations": "Concatenated with refers to the process of joining two sets of data end-to-end. In this context, it describes how the importance weights are combined with the already computed context annotations to form a unified vector."},
