{"han__detects__important_sentences_within_a_document": "The predicate 'detects' refers to the capability of the HAN model to identify and recognize elements within a text. In this context, it specifically pertains to the model's function of determining which sentences are significant within a document based on their context."},
{"important_sentences_within_a_document": "Important sentences within a document are those sentences that carry significant meaning or relevance in the context of the entire document. The HAN model is designed to identify these sentences by evaluating the context in which words and sentences appear, thus contributing to a more accurate document representation."},
{"han__considers__context": "The term 'considers' in this context refers to the HAN's approach of taking into account the varying importance of words and sentences based on their context within a document. This consideration is crucial for accurately encoding the document."},
