{"a_document_representation": "A document representation, in the context of HAN, is a structured encoding of a document that captures the importance of words and sentences within it. This representation is built through the construction of sentence vectors based on words and their aggregation using an attention mechanism."},
{"han__constructs__sentence_vectors_based_on_words": "The predicate \"constructs\" in this context refers to the process by which HAN builds or forms sentence vectors. This construction is a fundamental step in the model's approach to creating document representations, taking into account the importance of words and sentences within their contexts."},
{"sentence_vectors_based_on_words": "Sentence vectors based on words are representations of sentences that are derived from the words they contain. In the HAN model, these vectors are constructed to reflect the importance of each word within the sentence, considering the context in which the words appear. These vectors are then aggregated to form a document representation."},
{"han__aggregates__sentence_vectors_into_a_document_representation": "The term 'aggregates' in this context refers to the process by which HAN combines individual components\u2014in this case, sentence vectors\u2014into a unified representation. This aggregation is crucial for capturing the overall meaning and context of a document."},
