{"ann__has_recall__0_6747": "The predicate \"has_recall\" indicates the recall metric of the ANN model, which measures the model's ability to identify all relevant instances in the dataset."},
{"ann__has_f1_score__0_3958": "The predicate \"has_f1_score\" indicates that the subject, in this case, ANN, has been evaluated using the F1 score. The F1 score is a measure of a model's accuracy that considers both the precision and recall of the model. It is the harmonic mean of precision and recall, providing a balance between the two."},
{"0_3958": "The object \"0.3958\" represents the F1 score achieved by the ANN model in the given context. This score suggests a moderate level of performance, indicating that the model has some capability in balancing precision and recall for the task it was trained on."},
{"ann__has_roc_auc__0_6758": "The predicate \"has_roc_auc\" indicates that the subject, in this case, ANN, has a specific Receiver Operating Characteristic Area Under the Curve (ROC AUC) value, which is a performance measurement for classification problems at various threshold settings."},
{"0_6758": "The object \"0.6758\" is the ROC AUC value for the ANN model, indicating its performance in distinguishing between classes. A higher ROC AUC value suggests better performance, with 1 being a perfect score and 0.5 indicating a performance equivalent to random guessing."},
{"ann__has_pr_auc__0_6676": "The predicate \"has_pr_auc\" indicates that the subject, ANN, has a specific performance metric known as the Precision-Recall Area Under the Curve (PR AUC). This metric is used to evaluate the performance of a binary classifier, especially when the classes are imbalanced."},
{"0_6676": "The object \"0.6676\" represents the PR AUC score achieved by the ANN model. A PR AUC score of 0.6676 suggests that the model has a moderate ability to distinguish between positive and negative classes, with higher scores indicating better performance."},
{"ann__has_calibration_error__0_0782": "The predicate \"has_calibration_error\" indicates the presence of a calibration error in the ANN model. Calibration error measures how well the predicted probabilities from a model match the actual probabilities. A lower calibration error suggests that the model's confidence in its predictions is more aligned with the true likelihood of those predictions."},
{"0_0782": "The object \"-0.0782\" represents the calibration error value for the ANN model. This specific value suggests a relatively small calibration error, indicating that the ANN model's predicted probabilities are fairly well-calibrated, though there is still a slight discrepancy between predicted and actual probabilities."},
{"ann__has_calibration_slope__0_0605": "The predicate \"has_calibration_slope\" indicates the presence of a specific statistical measure associated with the ANN model. Calibration slope is a metric used to evaluate the reliability of probability predictions made by a model, assessing how well the predicted probabilities align with the actual outcomes."},
{"0_0605": "The object \"-0.0605\" represents the calibration slope value for the ANN model. A calibration slope close to 1 indicates well-calibrated predictions, whereas a value significantly different from 1 suggests that the model's probability predictions may be systematically over- or under-confident."},
