{"rf__f2_score_of__76_10": "The F2-score is a metric used to evaluate the performance of a machine learning model, particularly in imbalanced datasets. It places more emphasis on recall than precision, making it suitable for scenarios where false negatives are more costly than false positives."},
{"76_10": "76.10% is the F2-score achieved by the Random Forest model in the context of evaluating its performance using combined FIN and LING data. This score indicates the model's effectiveness in balancing precision and recall, with a slight preference towards recall."},
