{"highly_unbalanced": "Highly unbalanced refers to the disproportionate nature of fraud detection scenarios, where the number of fraudulent instances is significantly lower than non-fraudulent ones, making it challenging for models to accurately identify fraud."},
{"multiple_models": "Multiple models refer to various analytical frameworks or algorithms designed to detect and predict fraudulent activities. These models are tailored to capture different aspects of fraud, enhancing the overall detection capability."},
