{"different_signals": "Different signals in this context refer to the varied patterns, features, or indicators within financial and textual data that different machine learning models are able to detect and utilize for fraud detection. These signals can include specific words, phrases, financial ratios, or combinations thereof that suggest fraudulent activity."},
{"a_combination_of_models": "The subject refers to the integration of multiple models, which in this context are machine learning models used for fraud detection. These models include SVM, RF, and DL models, specifically the HAN architecture, which are employed to extract knowledge from financial and textual data."},
