{"indication_of_red_flags_words": "The indication of \u201cred-flags\u201d words refers to specific terms or phrases that are commonly associated with fraudulent activities or deceptive practices in financial documents. These words are typically used as signals by auditors and fraud detection models to identify potential cases of fraud."},
{"indication_of_red_flags_words__becoming__increasingly_unreliable_with_the_adaptive_response_of_the_alleged_offending_parties": "Becoming increasingly unreliable signifies a growing ineffectiveness or lack of dependability in the use of \u201cred-flags\u201d words as indicators of fraud. This unreliability is due to the adaptive strategies employed by those attempting to conceal fraudulent activities, making it harder to detect deception through simple keyword analysis."},
{"increasingly_unreliable_with_the_adaptive_response_of_the_alleged_offending_parties": "The adaptive response of the alleged offending parties refers to the actions taken by individuals or entities involved in fraudulent activities to modify their behavior and language in order to avoid detection. This might include changing the terminology used in financial documents or employing more sophisticated methods to obscure fraudulent practices."},
{"sentence_level_markup": "Sentence-level markup refers to the process of annotating or highlighting specific parts of sentences to provide additional context or information. In the context of fraud detection, it involves marking up sentences to indicate potential \"red-flag\" terms or phrases that may suggest fraudulent activity."},
