{"investigation__included__the_potential_of_accompanying_text_data_in_annual_reports": "The predicate \"included\" signifies that the research study encompassed or took into account certain elements or aspects within its scope. In this context, it indicates that the study incorporated specific components or considerations in its methodology or analysis."},
{"the_potential_of_accompanying_text_data_in_annual_reports": "The potential of accompanying text data in annual reports refers to the possibility or capability of utilizing the textual information found within annual financial reports to enhance the detection of financial fraud. This involves analyzing the linguistic content alongside quantitative data to identify signals or indicators of fraudulent activities within financial documentation."},
{"textual_analysis__has__increasing_significance_for_the_detection_of_signals_of_fraud_within_financial_documentation": "The predicate \"has\" in this context signifies the possession or attribution of a quality or characteristic. Here, it indicates that textual analysis possesses or is characterized by an increasing significance in the context of detecting signals of fraud within financial documentation."},
{"increasing_significance_for_the_detection_of_signals_of_fraud_within_financial_documentation": "The increasing significance for the detection of signals of fraud within financial documentation refers to the growing importance and relevance of using textual analysis methods to identify potential indicators of fraudulent activities in financial reports and documents."},
{"proposed_han_method": "The proposed HAN method is a state-of-the-art deep learning model designed to enhance financial fraud detection by analyzing both financial and linguistic information within textual data."},
{"proposed_han_method__concentrates_on__the_content_as_well_as_the_context_of_textual_information": "The predicate \"concentrates on\" indicates that the proposed HAN method specifically focuses its analysis and processing efforts on certain aspects of textual information, aiming to extract meaningful insights from them."},
{"the_content_as_well_as_the_context_of_textual_information": "The content as well as the context of textual information refers to the dual focus of the HAN method on both the explicit meanings and the surrounding circumstances or implications of words and phrases within a text, which is crucial for detecting subtle signals of fraud."},
{"bow_method__disregards__word_order_and_additional_grammatical_information": "The term \"disregards\" in this context means that the BOW method does not take into account or pay attention to certain aspects of text, specifically word order and additional grammatical information, when representing text as a collection of words."},
{"word_order_and_additional_grammatical_information": "Word order and additional grammatical information refer to the sequence of words in a sentence and the grammatical rules that govern their arrangement and relationship. This includes syntax, morphology, and other linguistic features that contribute to the meaning and structure of sentences."},
{"dl__is_capable_of__capturing_semantic_associations_and_discerning_the_meanings_of_different_word_and_phrase_combinations": "\"Is capable of\" indicates that DL has the inherent ability or functionality to perform a specific task or set of tasks. In this context, it highlights DL's advanced features compared to other methods like BOW (Bag of Words)."},
{"capturing_semantic_associations_and_discerning_the_meanings_of_different_word_and_phrase_combinations": "Capturing semantic associations and discerning the meanings of different word and phrase combinations refers to DL's ability to understand and interpret the relationships and nuances within text data. This capability allows DL to go beyond simple keyword matching and to comprehend the context and subtleties of language, making it particularly effective for tasks like fraud detection in textual data."},
{"dl_model__achieved__considerable_improvement_in_auc_compared_to_the_benchmark_models": "The predicate \"achieved\" indicates that the DL model successfully attained a specific level of performance in detecting financial fraud. This performance is measured against benchmark models, highlighting the effectiveness and superiority of the DL model in this context."},
{"considerable_improvement_in_auc_compared_to_the_benchmark_models": "The object \"considerable improvement in AUC compared to the benchmark models\" refers to the significant enhancement in the Area Under the Curve (AUC) metric achieved by the DL model. This improvement demonstrates the DL model's superior ability to correctly identify fraudulent cases over traditional machine learning models, which tend to perform better at identifying truthful statements."},
{"dl_model__is_well_suited_to__identify_the_fraudulent_cases_correctly": "The phrase \"is well suited to\" indicates that the DL model has a high level of appropriateness or effectiveness in performing a specific task. In this context, it suggests that the DL model is particularly effective in a certain application or scenario related to financial fraud detection."},
{"identify_the_fraudulent_cases_correctly": "Identifying fraudulent cases correctly refers to the capability of the DL model to accurately distinguish between fraudulent and non-fraudulent instances in financial documentation. This involves detecting signals of fraud within textual information, which is crucial for the effective detection of fraudulent firms."},
{"ml_models": "ML models refer to machine learning models, which are algorithms designed to learn patterns and make predictions or decisions based on data. In the context of financial fraud detection, these models are trained to analyze various types of data to identify potential fraudulent activities."},
{"ml_models__fail_to__detect_fraudulent_cases_while_performing_better_at_correctly_identifying_the_truthful_statements": "The phrase \"fail to\" indicates a shortcoming or limitation of the ML models in performing a specific task. In this case, it highlights the inability of most ML models to effectively detect fraudulent cases, despite their overall performance in correctly identifying truthful statements."},
{"detect_fraudulent_cases_while_performing_better_at_correctly_identifying_the_truthful_statements": "Detecting fraudulent cases while performing better at correctly identifying truthful statements refers to the dual challenge faced by ML models in financial fraud detection. It involves not only identifying instances of fraud but also maintaining a high level of accuracy in recognizing legitimate, non-fraudulent cases. The object highlights the specific area where ML models, in comparison to the DL model, exhibit limitations."},
{"detection_of_fraudulent_firms__is_of__great_importance": "The phrase \"is of\" in this context signifies the level of significance or importance attributed to the detection of fraudulent firms. It underscores the necessity and value placed on identifying and addressing financial fraud within the business environment."},
{"great_importance": "Great importance indicates the high level of priority and urgency associated with the detection of fraudulent firms. This importance is driven by the potential financial losses, erosion of investor confidence, and the overall negative impact on the economy that fraudulent activities can cause."},
{"mc": "MC, or Management Commentary, refers to the textual information provided by company management in financial reports, particularly in the Management Discussion and Analysis (MD&A) section. It is a critical component for stakeholders to understand the company's financial health and strategic direction."},
{"mc__is_associated_with__fraud": "The association between MC and fraud indicates a relationship where certain characteristics or patterns within the Management Commentary are linked to fraudulent activities. This relationship is significant in the context of fraud detection, suggesting that analyzing MC can help identify potential red flags or warning signals of fraudulent behavior."},
